# Intendex — rules for the Cursor agent

Project: market-data index of the AI agent economy (agents, MCP servers, A2A, pricing, capabilities, history).
Stack: Supabase (Postgres) + Edge Functions (Deno/TypeScript) for bots + Next.js (SSR) for the public site.

## Data rules — never break them
1. NO SOURCE -> NO CLAIM. Every fact has a source (sources.code, e.g. 'SRC-001'). Never write a fact without one.
2. NO EVIDENCE -> UNKNOWN. Never store null/false because data is missing. Missing = no row. UI shows "Not documented", never "No".
3. NO HISTORY -> NO CHANGE CLAIM. Never display a variation, trend or "+x%" without >= 2 real data points. Otherwise show "Baseline" / "New".
4. Keep declared / observed / derived separate (evidence_level). Our own probes = observed.
5. Score and Momentum are separate. Scores always show confidence + methodology version.
6. Never invent a capability, a price or a comparison. Comparisons are generated from database fields only.
7. Sponsored content (later) must always be clearly labeled "Sponsored".

## How to write data
- Bots NEVER insert into tables directly. Use the SQL functions: resolve_entity, record_observation,
  record_price, link, record_metric, compute_momentum, compute_agent_score.
- Bots run server-side only (Edge Functions + cron) with the service_role key. Never expose service_role to the browser.
- Each bot run opens a crawl_runs row (bot, source, counts, errors, cost) and closes it.
- Respect each source's legal field: sources.is_active = false or redistribution_allowed = false -> internal use only, never displayed.
- Rate-limit politely, respect robots.txt, store raw pages in Storage (snapshots table) with a sha256 content_hash; skip unchanged pages.

## Schema changes
- Add a new numbered migration in supabase/migrations/ (never edit an applied one).
- Run scripts/local_test.sh before pushing; tests must pass.
- Seeds are generated by scripts/build_seeds.py from data/source_map.csv — edit the CSV/taxonomy, not the SQL.

## Site (later)
- Public pages read only the v_* views and search_entities(). Server-rendered HTML, JSON-LD per page, canonical, sitemap.
- Don't create thin pages: a page is indexable only if its entity is published and has enough sourced data.
- Public site language: English.
